  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Echoing Green (EG) COVID 19 - Carbofix</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to use seed capital to fund the Anti-pollution Mask Program to offer low-income Nairobi residents subsidized masks. Residents who live in Africas largest slum, Kibera, are surrounded by poor air quality mainly caused by industrial plants. Due to the social distancing directive, issued by the Kenyan government, four million residents who reside low-income areas are facing difficulties adhering to this directive. As a result, many residents are in need of face masks and Jeremiah has decided to modify his anti-pollution masks to be used to control the spread of COVID-19.</narrative>
  </description>
